# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build.sh emits the binary at the repo root; the release workflow cross-compiles
# into dist/. These are anchored with a leading slash: as bare patterns they
# would match a file or directory of that name at ANY depth, so a future
# cmd/claude-playbook/ package would be silently dropped from the tree.
/claude-playbook
/cpb
/bin/test-cpb
/dist/

# Go toolchain artifacts. *.test is the compiled test binary -- it does not
# match *_test.go sources, which stay tracked.
*.exe
*.test
*.out
*.prof

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing matching these has ever been committed to this repo. The patterns
# exist so an accidental key or credential file cannot be staged in the first
# place -- a secret removed in a later commit still ships in every clone.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
*.gpg
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
credentials.json
secrets.json
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code runtime state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project creates and manages CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR trees, so a stray run with
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR pointed at the repo drops live session data here. Session
# transcripts (projects/) and edit snapshots (file-history/) record whatever a
# session touched, including credentials typed into commands -- they are the
# highest-value thing in the tree to keep out of git.
#
# Anchored to the repo root, which is where Claude Code actually writes, so
# these can never collide with a test fixture of the same name under tests/.
/projects/
/file-history/
/shell-snapshots/
/session-env/
/paste-cache/
/statsig/
/todos/
/history.jsonl
/.claude.json
/.claude.json.backup
/.credentials.json

# .claude/ holds project-scoped config. Ignore its contents (runtime state)
# while leaving room to track a shared settings.json deliberately: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so this excludes the
# directory's contents rather than the directory itself.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
